abstract: >-
  A unified, curated dataset of 3,693 literature-derived records on the
  hydrothermal conversion of biomass, centered on lignocellulosic and lignin-rich
  feedstocks (with mixed and boundary feedstocks also present), covering
  hydrothermal liquefaction, hydrothermal carbonization, solvothermal HTL and
  aqueous-phase reforming. It covers 433 biomass samples published between 1982
  and 2026. Each record is normalized to a standardized schema of 145 documented
  variables spanning source provenance, feedstock identity and composition,
  operating conditions, product yields, condensed-phase properties, energy and
  carbon allocation metrics, and derived descriptors, with provenance tracking,
  quality-control closure flags, and explicit imputation flags and methods.
  Source title and identifier are provided for every record; more granular
  Provenance and Ref information is retained where available. Version 1
  supersedes Version 0 and provides the complete publication dataset.
